der a universal set $X.$ Then, the indicator function of a set $A⊆X$ is the function\n\n$$\n{1}_{A}(x)={\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }x\\in A, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }x\\notin A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe indicator function of the set ${m,r,t}$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/1f/1fd2100d57c3483e737dc40298d4d5f61099ebc2863c54839906b66183acf576.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that the elements $m,r$ and $t$ (the elements of our subset) are mapped to $1,$ and all other elements are mapped to $0.$" 13194139534374 17592186045417 true] [17592186420399 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420397 13194139534374 17592186045417 true] [17592186420399 1069 "q-174368" 13194139534374 17592186045417 true] [17592186420399 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534374 17592186045417 true] [17592186420399 1071 "Which of the following is the indicator function ${1}_{A}(x)$ of the subset $A={2,4,8}$ of $X={0,2,4,6,8}.$" 13194139534374 17592186045417 true] [17592186420399 1072 #uuid "29b59535-24cf-5f4f-a890-c8446f20f105" 13194139534374 17592186045417 true] [17592186420399 1074 "An indicator function maps elements from a set to the values $0$ or $1,$ depending on whether the element belongs to a specified subset. The indicator function is designed to \"indicate\" whether an element is a member of a subset.\n\nMore specifically, consider a universal set $X.$ Then, the indicator function of a set $A⊆X$ is the function\n\n$$\n{1}_{A}(x)={\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }x\\in A, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }x\\notin A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe indicator function of the set ${2,4,8}$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/85/850019897d92b0a8d3340c091cee15342be20e99e7578a9fca23f88804e3bf28.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that the elements $2,4$ and $8$ (the elements of our subset) are mapped to $1,$ and all other elements are mapped to $0.$" 13194139534374 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-03fbd85f-b443-5e0c-9c2a-949a37212341" 17592186420386 "answer-065f51d0-87f5-5d0a-beff-e1ffeb43d4fd" 17592186420387 "answer-133bd8dc-2c5b-5e1b-bfb2-e4928c76cb5